  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Access to Water and Sanitation in Karonga District</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Karonga, 45% of people lack access to clean water and 89% lack adequate sanitation facilities. This has a significant impact on health and well being. This project will improve access to safe drinking water by rehabilitating 7 out of use water points, and establishing 4 new water points. Sanitation will be improved by constructing 62 latrines with hand washing facilities in 5 schools and 2 clinics.  Hygiene practices will be enhanced through health &amp; hygiene messaging and the establishment of 5 School Health Clubs. Water Point Committees and pump minders will be trained to maintain infrastructure, to ensure sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
